.SH NAME
MediaKeySession.keystatuseschange_event \- MediaKeySession:
keystatuseschange event
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]keystatuseschange\f[B]\f[R] event of the
\f[CR]MediaKeySession\f[R] API fires when there has been a change in the
keys or their statuses within a session.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqkeystatuseschange\(dq, (event) => { })

onkeystatuseschange = (event) => { }
.EE
